    en: "Djurdjura National Park is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Algeria. High peaks and home to Barbary macaques. Barbary macaques. High peaks. Natural landscape. This protected area is part of Algeria's diverse wildlife and flora, from the Sahara to the Tell Atlas. Like many notable places in Algeria, it combines Berber heritage with Mediterranean and Saharan influences. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Algeria."
